  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1984-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have \\(x-\\frac1y=\\frac{xy-1}{y}\\) and \\(y-\\frac1x=\\frac{xy-1}{x}.\\) The hypotheses make the needed quantities nonzero, so their quotient is \\[ \\frac{\\frac{xy-1}{y}}{\\frac{xy-1}{x}}=\\frac{x}{y}. \\] Therefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Write the numerator and denominator as single fractions",
        "Both parts contain the common factor \\(xy-1\\)"
      ],
